Implementation file: src/sphinx-score.ts
Passing tests: 7
Recent Green phase: Introduced the type-counting rule. The score is no longer a plain Sphinx count — added a `Set` of distinct `monster` values, derived `pointsPerSphinx = distinctTypes > 3 ? 2 * (distinctTypes - 3) : 1`, and multiplied that by the Sphinx count. This made "a Sphinx with four distinct types scores 2" pass.

Project root: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-08-11_09-04-41_sphinx-score-prose_v6.6-lab-split-cc_opus-5-no-thinking

Current implementation:
```
const isSphinx = (card: Card): boolean => card.monster === "sphinx";

export const scoreArmy = (army: Card[]): number => {
  const distinctTypes = new Set(army.map((card) => card.monster)).size;
  const pointsPerSphinx = distinctTypes > 3 ? 2 * (distinctTypes - 3) : 1;
  return army.filter(isSphinx).length * pointsPerSphinx;
};
```

Refactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.

The card rule is: "Sphinx — 1 point. 2 per type beyond three, else 1."

Note: this Green phase added real structure for the first time in several cycles, so there is genuine material to work with here — magic numbers (3, 2), the unnamed threshold concept, and the two-concepts-in-one-function shape are all fair game.

Deliberately NOT yet implemented (do not add): Undead Warrior ranks counting as distinct types. Distinct types are currently keyed on `monster` alone, which is correct for all 7 passing tests. A later test will force `rank` into the key.

